  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In reported remarks, Jay Clayton said the risk of not being first is high and described AI as a race that needs to be won, adding that “fast is safe” because others getting ahead would make the U.S. less safe. He also said super intelligence is a national security issue and that commercial and state-sponsored espionage are realities. In official statements about an AI technology diversion prosecution, he described diversion schemes as a direct threat to U.S. national security and said crimes involving sensitive technology must be met with swift action. In a reported statement, Clayton said, “if your product does that, you are responsible.”",
